 1 big thing: Jeffries&#x27; Day 1 plans 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: CNN With 10 weeks until midterms, House Minority Leader Hakeem Jeffries (D-N.Y.) gave CNN's Wolf Blitzer a preview yesterday of what to expect should Democrats regain control of the House:

 "Hold every single member of the Trump cartel accountable." "Make sure that we've got people in government focused on doing the things necessary to address the affordability crisis." On impeachment, "we haven't ruled anything in and we haven't ruled anything out," with any move guided by "moments of accountability." That aligns with the priorities Jeffries has pushed on the stump : 

 Lower the cost of living. Make health care affordable. Take the Trump administration to task. ⚖️ Jeffries' careful line on impeachment underscores his challenge if he becomes speaker, with one wing of his caucus pushing to aggressively confront President Trump, while the other is desperate to avoid another impeachment fight, Axios' Andrew Solender reports. 

 The most pro-impeachment Democrats from Trump's first term have fallen in recent primaries. But lawmakers still see momentum behind trying again. "There are plenty of good reasons that Trump should be impeached based on his actions," a senior House Democrat told Axios. 🤷 The real question is political. Some Democrats aren't convinced it's worth pursuing again when two prior impeachments failed to stop Trump's return to the White House.

 "I believe that we will not do impeachment again," a second senior House Democrat said. "It's a major time suck — and will do nothing to forward our agenda." That lawmaker added that it "depends if we win the Senate." Democrats won't get close to the 67 votes needed to convict Trump in a party-line vote. State of play: Jeffries' balancing act is already causing him headaches. He faced blowback from some fellow Democrats this week after meeting with Trump's son-in-law, Jared Kushner.

 He defended the meeting in a video posted to social media, saying that Kushner "asked for a meeting, and I took it, to discuss the affordability crisis." Share this story ... More Dem reaction to the Kushner meeting . 

 
 
