 4. 🥇 Graham&#x27;s big night 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Sen. Darline Graham speaks at a victory event last night in Columbia, S.C. Photo: Megan Varner/Getty Images Sen. Darline Graham (R-S.C.), President Trump's pick, won the Republican nomination last night to fill the South Carolina Senate vacancy created by her brother Lindsey Graham's death.

 Why it matters: Her victory (52.5%–47.5%) underscores Trump's sway with Republican voters — and positions Graham as the odds-on favorite to win a full term in November.

 Her abbreviated primary campaign benefited from the president's endorsement, incumbency and one of the most recognizable names in South Carolina politics. 🤑 In addition to Trump hitting the trail with Graham on Friday, his MAGA Inc. made a last-minute push for her, spending more than $827,000 on calls and texts ahead of the vote, according to FEC reports.

