 8. 1 worthy read: NYT&#x27;s Afghan evac 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The New York Times' group deplanes from a military plane provided by Qatar in Mexico City. Photo: Najim Rahim A new book from journalists Rebecca Blumenstein and Diana Kapp provides crucial details about how The New York Times evacuated hundreds of Afghan nationals as the country fell to Taliban rule in 2021.

 "The Last Free Women," out next month just after the fifth anniversary of the fall of Afghanistan, explains how The Times' management and reporters helped identify and relocate more than 200 people fleeing the conflict, 124 of whom ended up in the U.S. "When you have a bureau like that, you have drivers who for years had taken our reporters around the country, translators, cooks ... really anyone who took care of the bureau for over 20 years," Blumenstein told Axios' Sara Fischer in an interview. 

 "They had a lot to fear because they knew that they were associated with The New York Times, and that with a Taliban takeover, they could be hunted down." Preorder the book ... Share this story . 

 
 
